    ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\text{det}(X)$, if\n    $X=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(X) & =|\\begin{aligned}10 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =10\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =40-(-3) \\\\  & =43\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
