    ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\text{det}(L)$, if\n    $L=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(L) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =12-(-10) \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$"
